rawler is licensed LGPL-2.1 (a copyleft licence, permitted for this project). It is used
unmodified as a normal Cargo dependency, so you can replace it with your own build of rawler.

option-ext (MPL-2.0, pulled in by directories) is file-level copyleft; it is used
unmodified as a normal Cargo dependency, so you can replace it with your own build.
The reqwest HTTP client uses rustls (no OpenSSL); the keyring crate talks to the Windows
Credential Manager, the macOS Keychain and the Linux Secret Service.
With no keychain, the token file is encrypted with the RustCrypto chacha20poly1305 and hkdf
crates (MIT OR Apache-2.0), with random bytes from getrandom (MIT OR Apache-2.0); key
material is wiped after use with zeroize (Apache-2.0 OR MIT). httpmock, tempfile and
filetime are development-only and are not shipped.
SQLite (bundled statically by libsqlite3-sys) is in the public domain.
epaint_default_fonts bundles unmodified fonts: Hack (MIT), Noto Emoji (SIL Open Font
Licence 1.1), Ubuntu-Light (Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0) and emoji-icon-font (MIT).
self_cell (Apache-2.0 OR GPL-2.0-only) and r-efi (MIT OR Apache-2.0 OR LGPL-2.1-or-later)
are used under Apache-2.0. egui_kittest is development-only and is not shipped.
strum and strum_macros (MIT) are development-only (test assertions) and are not shipped.
rfd (file dialogs): on Linux the picker uses the XDG desktop portal over D-Bus (libdbus is
loaded at run time, not linked) and falls back to zenity; there is no GTK. Windows uses the
common dialogs and macOS the open panel. Typing a folder path always works, with or without
a picker.

The AI tools (lf-ai) load ONNX Runtime (MIT, Microsoft) at run time from its official
release, downloaded on first use and checked by SHA-256; it is not linked or shipped. The
models are downloaded the same way and run on this computer: IS-Net general use (Apache-2.0),
SkySeg (MIT), SCUNet (Apache-2.0), Real-ESRGAN general x4v3 (BSD-3-Clause), LaMa
(Apache-2.0) and YuNet (MIT).
libwebp-sys builds Google's libwebp (BSD-3-Clause) from source into the program for lossy
WebP export; AVIF export uses rav1e and ravif (BSD-2-Clause / BSD-3-Clause), pure Rust.
webbrowser opens links (Help > About) in the system browser.
winresource (MIT) is build-only on Windows: it embeds the program icon and version
information into the .exe and is not itself shipped.
